WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.750
The one piece manga just confirmed one of
THE MOST GAME-CHANGING theories about Luffy’s

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.750
father.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.400
Ladies and gentlemen, Monkey D. Dragon was
a marine.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.870
That's right.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:17.779
Which means we simply must ask all sorts of
questions such as why did he join?

00:00:17.779 --> 00:00:18.779
What rank was he?

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:21.060
Did he already have his devil fruit?

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.610
What made him hate the world nobles SO MUCH
that he eventually declared war on the Celestial

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:27.610
Dragons?

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.189
And how did he become the MOST WANTED MAN
in the world?

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:33.380
Man, there’s so much to think about.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.970
But thankfully the chapter gave us some reason
why he left, which is that he realized that

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.440
there was no true justice there, but COME
ON.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.879
There has to be some truly tragic or horrifyingly
awful event that sparked his desire to leave.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:53.840
And honestly, by looking at his entire timeline
I think we can actually figure out what that

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.559
super important event might be.

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:00.199
Before we get ahead of ourselves though, let’s
start at the beginning here on this handy

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:06.200
timeline because to really understand Dragon’s
motivations we need to understand exactly

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.759
where he has been.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:15.479
It all starts when Dragon was born 55 years
ago, and we assume that Vice-Admiral Garp

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:19.890
is his father, even though that’s actually
never been confirmed.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:25.189
In fact, Garp only ever said that Dragon was
Luffy’s father, not that Dragon was his

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:29.659
own son, so there’s definitely room to speculate
that Garp is not Dragon’s dad.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:32.080
But for now, let’s assume that he is Garp’s
son.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.110
Well, then it makes a ton of sense that Garp
would want Dragon to join the marines, just

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.150
like he wanted Luffy to.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:45.950
Only this time it seems that Dragon listened
to Garp instead of immediately rebelling like

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:46.950
Luffy did.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:51.360
And I’m sure Garp was absolutely thrilled
that his son was following in his footsteps,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.020
but I also don’t think Dragon joined just
because of Garp.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:02.880
I mean, he clearly has a strong sense of justice
that he has continued to believe in even after

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.780
leaving the marines, so there must have been
some inner motivation for Dragon to join the

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.780
marines.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:15.220
Now while we don’t actually know when he
joined I think it’s reasonable to assume

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:20.860
that it was sometime as a late teenager or
early twenties, which just happens to line

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.360
up with the God Valley incident.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:29.700
More specifically Dragon was seventeen during
the events on God Valley, so maybe he joined

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.350
up soon after that enormous battle.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.370
Now, what exactly happened during his time
in the marines?

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:41.409
We don’t really know for sure, but he simply
must have risen high enough in the ranks to

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:44.260
realize there is no true justice there.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.720
Because he probably isn’t finding out something
life-changing like that as a common marine

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:57.019
or even lower ranking officer, so I would
imagine he became pretty high ranked, probably

00:02:57.019 --> 00:03:04.340
at least a Vice-Admiral if not even an Admiral
since those are the marines who get tasked

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.940
with a lot of the marine’s dirty work.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:16.010
And man, I would just love to see Marine Admiral
Dragon doing something truly amazing.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:22.390
Plus Dragon has this whole green color scheme
with his robe and clothing, so he would fit

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.730
right into the admiral’s color themes.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:35.599
But the next actual confirmed sighting of
Dragon is this scene right here, which was

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:41.069
sixteen years after the events of God Valley
when Dragon was thirty-three years old.

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:44.980
Now, at this point he has already left the
marines and formed what he calls the “Freedom

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.090
Fighters” which we’ll talk more about
in just a minute.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:54.200
However, when I read this scene it seems like
these Freedom Fighters have not been around

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:59.769
for all that long, so I would imagine that
Dragon was a marine until at least his late

00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:04.650
twenties, so maybe about five years or so
before this scene with Vegapunk.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:10.090
But even more importantly this scene gives
us our most concrete clue about why Dragon

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:15.680
may have grown to hate the Celestial Dragons
and eventually leave the marines.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.419
Before I speculate on that though, let’s
explain why some other common reasons for

00:04:19.419 --> 00:04:24.710
Dragon’s hatred of the world nobles are
probably not true at this point.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:29.660
One of the most common theories for Dragon’s
hatred was that the world nobles killed Luffy’s

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.660
mother.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.039
But after this chapter we can pretty much
cross out that idea because if you look up

00:04:35.039 --> 00:04:41.620
when Luffy was born, Dragon was already thirty-six
years old which is DEFINITELY AFTER he left

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:42.620
the marines.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:48.940
So that means Luffy was born AFTER Dragon
created the revolutionary army, which actually

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:56.300
brings back the idea that Ginny might be Luffy’s
mom, but more on that in just a minute.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.949
First, though another common idea for Dragon
hating the world nobles is the idea that he

00:05:00.949 --> 00:05:03.259
learned about the World’s secret ruler,
Imu.

00:05:03.259 --> 00:05:08.060
But this was basically already proven to be
false in chapter 1086.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:12.890
That’s because when Sabo explained that
Imu is the secret ruler of the world to Dragon

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:19.600
and Ivankov, there was absolutely no hint
that Dragon already knew this information.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:25.570
Which of course it is possible he was hiding
that info, but I think that’s pretty unlikely

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.570
at this point.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:29.910
So that’s also not the reason he left the
marines.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:36.560
So that leaves only two or three decent reasons
that I can see for Dragon leaving the marines.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.139
The first is that the world nobles didn’t
actually kill Luffy’s mom, but instead they

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:42.830
killed DRAGON’S mom.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:47.940
Which if we are going with the idea that Garp
is his actual father then that would mean

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.710
they killed Garp’s wife.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:54.960
Which again, seems pretty unlikely because
I feel like an event like that would send

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.639
Garp on a rampage to wipe out the world nobles
himself.

00:05:58.639 --> 00:06:03.490
Of course, if Dragon isn’t Garp’s son,
then we have a whole different situation,

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.990
but I still think this is unlikely.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:13.100
But the MOST LIKELY option based on the timeline
and the events from chapter 1066 is that at

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:19.450
some point Dragon met the scholars of Ohara
AND learned some of the true history of the

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:20.450
world.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:21.450
Don’t believe me?

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:25.750
Well, during his meeting with Vegapunk, Dragon
revealed that he already knew Professor Clover,

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:30.940
who was the leader of the scholars and was
desperately searching for information about

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.080
the Void Century.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:37.720
In fact, we were told in that same chapter
that Clover was arrested by the marines at

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.199
least ten times.

00:06:39.199 --> 00:06:44.569
So wouldn’t it just make a lot of sense
if Dragon was the one who chased after Clover

00:06:44.569 --> 00:06:48.349
while he was a marine.

00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:53.180
And if that was the case, I can easily imagine
that Dragon would become friends with the

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:58.099
adventurous scholar and even learn some of
the dark secrets about the world government

00:06:58.099 --> 00:07:00.680
that Clover discovered.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:05.260
I mean that same marine and pirate dynamic
is what happened to Garp and the former pirate

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:10.349
king, Gol D. Roger, where Garp chased after
Roger for years and they eventually became

00:07:10.349 --> 00:07:11.960
somewhat like friends.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:18.860
On top of all this, Dragon could have met
Nico Olvia, who was also one of the scholars

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:23.729
of Ohara and Robin’s mother.

00:07:23.729 --> 00:07:29.289
In fact, in chapter 593 we learned that the
Revolutionary Army and Dragon have been searching

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:35.190
for Robin for over ten years and they even
call her “the Light of the Revolution”.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:39.379
Which is just even more evidence that Dragon
had an important relationship with Clover

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:45.530
or Olvia in the past, and it fits together
nicely that this relationship plus maybe some

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:51.280
other tragic event sparked Dragon’s desire
to defeat the Celestial Dragons.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:57.090
Or one more bonus option is that Dragon met
Roger at some point and learned the true history

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.530
of the world.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:04.110
This is possible because Roger did find Laugh
Tale about three years before Dragon met with

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.409
Vegapunk right here.

00:08:05.409 --> 00:08:10.349
So I’m just saying, the timing lines up
pretty well.

00:08:10.349 --> 00:08:18.289
Plus I’ve always been super curious how
Dragon earned the highest bounty in the entire

00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:19.289
world.

00:08:19.289 --> 00:08:24.069
And while we don’t find out in this chapter,
we do know that the ONE THING the world government

00:08:24.069 --> 00:08:45.690
absolutely does not allow is 
the 

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.710
research into the poneglyphs.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:53.209
So if Dragon was friends with the people who
did research the poneglyphs or he got some

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:57.959
info about them from Roger, then all of that
plus the fact that he is making an entire

00:08:57.959 --> 00:09:09.550
army to fight the world nobles could be enough
for him to earn that super high bounty.

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:14.540
But whichever of these reasons sparked Dragon’s
decision to leave the marines, it’s not

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.480
as important as what happens next.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:23.660
Because as we learned from chapter 1066, Dragon
had already formed a group known as the Freedom

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:28.560
Fighters, which is essentially Dragon’s
group of rebels before he officially formed

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.940
the Revolutionary Army.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:34.850
And in this most recent chapter we finally
get to see these Freedom Fighters in action.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:40.160
That’s because about sixteen years after
Kuma and Ginny started living on the island,

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:45.490
the ruler of the Sorbet kingdom basically
segregated the entire island into a section

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:51.310
protected by the kingdom and a section that
is just lawless land.

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:57.079
On top of this, there was a MASSIVE tax placed
on the people to pay for the World Government’s

00:09:57.079 --> 00:09:58.079
heavenly tribute.

00:09:58.079 --> 00:10:03.660
Now, this whole storyline might finally explain
how Kuma got his reputation as the “Tyrant

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.680
King” because even though he is basically
a priest for these people I can honestly see

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:13.100
the young Kuma rising up to become sort of
the boss or king of the lawless land, which

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:18.720
obviously the upper class of this kingdom
wouldn’t want at all, and he is put into

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.720
jail.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:24.720
But soon after that Dragon and Ivankov arrived
with their band of Freedom Fighters to overthrow

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:29.959
this corrupt ruler, which leads to Kuma and
Ginny joining up with the Freedom fighters,

00:10:29.959 --> 00:10:34.370
which then officially became the Revolutionary
Army.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:40.350
From here though, there are a few new important
points we can add to our timeline.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:45.839
For example, in this chapter we learned that
fourteen years ago Kuma and Ginny were confirmed

00:10:45.839 --> 00:10:49.180
to both still be a part of the Revolutionaries.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:53.010
At this time, Kuma is thirty-three years old
and Ginny is thirty-seven.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:57.440
And this fact by itself is super surprising.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:01.560
First of all, again, props to Ginny for surviving
this long.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:06.350
I honestly thought she wouldn’t make it
off of God Valley, but the second interesting

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:11.910
point this brings up is that we once again
have to reanalyze the question of if Ginny

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:13.440
is someone’s mother.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:18.420
After last chapter it seemed pretty logical
that since she and Kuma were living together

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:24.240
then Ginny would eventually be Bonney’s
mom, and I’d still say that is the most

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:29.200
likely option since Ginny already wanted to
marry Kuma in this chapter.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:33.480
I mean there is just so much similarity between
their names and personalities.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.779
But WAIT until you hear the INSANE theory
coming up in just a moment.

00:11:37.779 --> 00:11:42.880
Before that though, another option is Ginny
being Luffy’s mom, which after last chapter

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:48.310
I thought that wouldn’t be the case, but
now that she has been fully with the revolutionaries

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:53.780
for such a long time, I mean anything could
have happened between Ginny and Kuma or Ginny

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:54.780
and Dragon.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:59.500
Which, okay, is just such a weird love triangle
to even think about.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:02.430
So, onto the next option.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:07.790
Then there is of course the idea that Bonney
is Ginny’s clone, but now that we learned

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:12.101
at the end of this chapter that Ginny has
been kidnapped, I am starting to think there

00:12:12.101 --> 00:12:17.850
might be a mind-blowing new possibility that
we hadn’t considered.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:22.790
Because even though we don’t know exactly
when on the timeline that Ginny was kidnapped,

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:28.010
we can reasonably guess that it was sometime
around fourteen years before the current story.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:33.100
And whenever this occurred it gives us the
perfect set up for Kuma to become a Warlord

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.640
and World Government slave.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:40.029
Because if Ginny was captured by the World
Government then OF COURSE Kuma is going to

00:12:40.029 --> 00:12:41.529
try and save her.

00:12:41.529 --> 00:12:45.910
Maybe they wanted Ginny for some sort of devil
fruit power or some other reason, but for

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.269
now that reason isn’t that important.

00:12:48.269 --> 00:12:51.540
Honestly, I keep saying I’ve been surprised
that Ginny has been alive for this long, but

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:56.430
what if that is because she was never actually
dead in the first place.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:13:03.139
That’s right, I’m saying that the Bonney
that we have known for most of the story is

00:13:03.139 --> 00:13:09.130
in fact Ginny who was aged down AND had her
memories pushed out by Kuma.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.910
Which sounds CRAZY!

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:16.139
I know, and while she doesn’t look exactly
like Bonney in this chapter her appearance

00:13:16.139 --> 00:13:18.320
isn’t far off.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:23.980
Plus if you look deep enough, there is some
pretty solid evidence that supports this idea.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:28.480
First of all, we know the world government
wanted Bonney’s for some reason and it appears

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.130
they once had her captured.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:35.330
Which seems really odd seeing as how we’ve
always viewed Bonney as a pirate and a pretty

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:41.470
young one at that, but what if they had captured
her as Ginny and then they later let her go

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:44.930
in exchange for Kuma becoming the world government’s
slave?

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:50.510
On top of that, if you look back to chapter
1074 and the memories that Bonney viewed in

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:55.380
the lab, there are some very odd circumstances
surrounding this.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:14:00.240
First of all, Vegapunk was desperate for Bonney
not to see those memories, which was always

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.940
a bit weird to me.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:06.270
I mean yeah, her father’s memories might
have been painful, but wouldn’t it be good

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:08.839
for Bonney to see what her father went through?

00:14:08.839 --> 00:14:14.070
Unless of course those actually weren’t
Kuma’s memories, but they were instead Ginny’s

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:18.399
memories and Veapunk didn’t want her to
realize that Bonney isn’t who she thought

00:14:18.399 --> 00:14:19.490
she is.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:24.450
Also, in this flashback that we thought was
Kuma’s, Bonney is looking at Kuma from the

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:29.370
outside, which wouldn’t make sense if they
were Kuma’s memories.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:34.360
If these were Kuma’s memories, shouldn’t
the memories show a perspective through his

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:35.360
own eyes?

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:42.100
Instead, we see it as if someone else is looking
at Kuma, which would make sense if these were

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.100
Ginny’s memories.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:47.779
Plus, we were also literally shown Bonney
turning Vegapunk into a baby right before

00:14:47.779 --> 00:14:51.490
she touched the memories, which seems like
some sort of foreshadowing that Oda would

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:52.490
do.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:58.750
However, the evidence that fits this theory
all together is this panel from chapter 908.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:03.670
So in case you don’t remember, this scene
had Bonney trying to sneak into Mary Geoise

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.000
in order to save Kuma.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.529
But going back to look at it now, I just have
to wonder how she knew who this Conney person

00:15:09.529 --> 00:15:12.630
was and that they were the Dowager Queen of
Kuma’s homeland.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:18.370
Unless of course she once lived there and
had memories of this person, just like Ginny

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.370
did.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:23.149
Plus there is the question of how she even
looks enough like this Conney person to fool

00:15:23.149 --> 00:15:28.040
the guards, but I don’t have an answer for
that unless Ginny was a descendant of that

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:32.690
ruling family or something, which doesn’t
seem like the case from this chapter.

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:39.190
But yeah, Ginny might be a mother, but she
also might also still be alive as Bonney and

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:41.389
we never knew it.

00:15:41.389 --> 00:15:47.360
But with all this talk of Dragon, the marines,
and the revolutionaries, I do wonder if Dragon’s

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:52.120
story of being a marine and later leaving
will be the model for another marine to flip

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.420
sides in the future.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:57.360
An easy choice for this character would be
Koby, but honestly I see him more as following

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.489
in Garp’s footsteps than Dragon’s.

00:15:59.489 --> 00:16:04.040
I mean, Koby literally dreams of being a marine
admiral, and he trained under Garp.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:08.920
Plus Garp basically gave up his life to save
Koby, so yeah, I see Koby as trying to get

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:12.750
rid of the corruption from within the marines
rather than from the outside.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:17.120
Which means the perfect candidate is Vice-Admiral
Smoker.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:22.220
I mean, if you look at his entire character
arc which has just led to him uncovering more

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:26.709
and more government corruption then it would
make sense that eventually he wouldn’t be

00:16:26.709 --> 00:16:30.750
able to take any more and he will choose to
leave the marines.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:35.940
At this point, I just wonder what event might
tip him over the edge and make him possibly

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:38.460
become a pirate or join the revolutionaries.

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:42.630
What’s even more exciting though is that
the flashback is not even over yet, so in

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:47.199
the next few chapters we might even get to
